Found by the k181 worker, pre-existing. Where a sync cannot write (a file where a directory should go, say), the Perl engine reports `mkpath failed for <path>: File exists`; the reference reports Node's errno text (`EEXIST: file already exists, mkdir '<path>'` and the like). The report line and the hook systemMessage differ in bytes.

Decide per error class whether to word them as Node does (a small errno -> code/syscall table in Skilletor::FSUtil) or to note the divergence under engines.perl in the cases that hit it. A conformance case for one write error first.
